* Murata chip ferrite beads.
* BEAD26 (BLM18KG260TN1) is fitted on the board; BEAD120 (BLM18KG121TH1, the part on TI's EVM) is kept for comparison.
*
* BLM18KG121TH1 chip ferrite bead, 120 ohm at 100 MHz, 3 A, 0603
* Equivalent circuit with the element values of Murata's published SPICE model for this part
* (valid 1 MHz - 3 GHz, 25 C, no DC bias, small signal).  The series inductances are scaled by
* the parameter k so that the loss of inductance under DC bias can be swept: a ferrite bead
* carrying a large share of its rated current keeps only a fraction of its small-signal value.
* R4 is the DC resistance (22 mohm typical, 30 mohm maximum in the datasheet).
.subckt BEAD120 a b params: k=1 rdc=0.022
R1 a 1 103.2
L1 a 1 {1.925e-7*k}
C1 a 2 1.158e-12
R2 1 2 26.11
L2 1 2 {4.165e-7*k}
R3 2 3 21.78
L3 2 3 {1.224e-7*k}
R4 3 b {rdc}
.ends BEAD120

* BLM18KG260TN1 chip ferrite bead, 26 ohm at 100 MHz, 6 A, 0603, 7 mohm maximum DC resistance.
* Element values of Murata's published SPICE model; inductances scaled by k as above.
.subckt BEAD26 a b params: k=1 rdc=0.004
R1 a 1 3.521
L1 a 1 {4.838e-8*k}
C1 a 2 2.539e-12
R2 1 2 4.901
L2 1 2 {6.735e-8*k}
R3 2 3 20.79
L3 2 3 {5.137e-8*k}
R4 3 b {rdc}
.ends BEAD26
